  "rules": [
    "Model exhibits severe upward bias when recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., prices dropping from ~74 to ~66) followed by neutral sentiment; forecasts consistently overshoot true outcomes by 3-5%.",
    "Forecasts fail to capture high-frequency volatility spikes, predicting smooth linear growth while true outcomes show sharp V-shapes or sudden reversals within the first 10 days.",
    "When sentiment history contains mixed signals (positive and negative values) amidst a volatile price range, the model defaults to a conservative mean-reversion path that underestimates upside potential.",
    "The forecast horizon is systematically too long-term; actual outcomes often peak or bottom out within the first 7-14 days, whereas the model projects gradual drift over the full 30-day period.",
    "In periods of high sentiment volatility (sentiment > 0.5), the model's confidence in its upward trajectory is misplaced, leading to significant negative tracking error as true prices fluctuate wildly."
  ]
}
